c,\" a term for Japanese pop music from the 1920s to the 1980s) in the Japanese music scene.  The term was coined by the Japanese media to distinguish Japanese music from foreign music, and now refers to most Japanese popular music.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Ado", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Aimer", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Fujii Kaze", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "King Gnu", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Lisa", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "RADWIMPS", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Red Velvet", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "TWICE", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Vaundy", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "YOASOBI", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "ZUTOMAYO", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "tuki.", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "jazz": {"genre": "jazz", "country_code": "tw", "country_name": "Taiwan", "summary": "Jazz is a musical art form which originated around the beginning of the 20th century in Black communities in the Southern United States from a confluence of African and European music traditions. The style's West African pedigree is evident in its use of blue notes, call-and-response, improvisation, polyrhythms, syncopation, and the swung note of ragtime.\n\nFrom its early development until the present, jazz has also incorporated music from 19th and 20th century American popular music, which is based on European music traditions.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": 19361, "best_position": 60}, {"artist": "Fujii Kaze", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Kendrick Lamar", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Laufey", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Lauv", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Stev